    "narrative": "For LawDog, today\u2019s lineup is anchored by the dual threat of **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52). **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter against Javier, where an excellent park factor and an elite SP matchup push his efficiency into the top tier. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in a prime spot against Martinez, N; his score is bolstered by a potent combination of strong park dimensions and a 17% SP skill boost, making him a high-ceiling play. **Jonathan Aranda** also demands attention at 68.94, as he exploits a soft matchup against Baz; his 16% park boost and the order #2 placement make him our most reliable anchor for run production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose score of 50.65 made him a difficult exclusion. While his projected speed metrics\u2014critical for our scarcity-focused strategy\u2014are valuable, he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Gavin Sheets** and **Justin Crawford**, both of whom are better positioned to capitalize on their respective SP matchups. **Brendan Donovan** is the primary point of concern in today's set; facing an elite arm in Imanaga (3.69 xERA), his platoon disadvantage pushes his score down to a marginal 41.39. With his lineup spot still pending, he remains the most volatile asset in our daily structure.\n\nWe are navigating a high-risk landscape with **Cal Raleigh** (53.80) and **Brendan Donovan** (41.39), both of whom are staring down the talented Imanaga. While **Cal Raleigh** retains enough power upside to warrant a start, his lack of official lineup confirmation and the tough SP draw limit his ceiling. By contrast, **Bryce Harper** (66.02) remains a stable cornerstone, buoyed by a strong xwOBA profile and a favorable matchup against Leahy. We will continue to monitor the weather and official order reports, particularly for **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan**, to ensure we aren't burning valuable game caps on sub-optimal platoon configurations.",
